   "question": "The context above covers the motivation for anisotropic absorbers, the hypothesis about oriented growth, the quasi-2D Sn-Pb perovskite composition, and the one-step spin-coating deposition. Using panel F1e for the additive-grown film, what feature appears in the diffraction map, roughly where is it positioned, and what does the corresponding intensity profile taken along that same direction look like?",
   "answer_key": "The diffraction map for the additive-grown film shows a single distinct (202) feature lying on the out-of-plane direction at roughly 20 nm^-1; the intensity profile taken along that same out-of-plane direction shows one sharp, well-defined feature at that same position, indicating a single dominant signal rather than a ring or multiple scattered features.",
